course: dictionary
lesson: 12837
title: Magic words and charming people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stories often have a magic character, and the words around them tell you what that character does. «The wicked enchanter waved his staff and cast a spell.» Wicked tells you he is bad, and a spell is magic, so an enchanter must be someone who uses magic.
explain: «The enchantress could break the spell, but only at midnight.» The girl version of an enchanter is an enchantress. Both words come from magic, so when you see either one, look for spells, castles, potions or secrets nearby.
explain: Words can also be used in a different way. «Grandma is such an enchanter with her stories that we never want her to stop.» Grandma is not using magic here. She charms and delights people, so enchanter means someone who holds you spellbound.
fact: An enchanter is a person in stories who uses magic spells.
fact: «Enchanter» can also describe someone who charms and delights people, not just a magic person.
fact: The female form is «enchantress», and the plural is «enchanters».
fact: «Merlin» is often called an enchanter in old legends.
fact: Good context clues for enchanter are spell, magic, wicked, potion and charm.
exercise: «The wicked enchanter waved his staff and cast a spell.» What is an enchanter in this sentence? | A stone wall in a castle | *A person who uses magic spells | A kind old teacher | A type of horse
exercise: «The enchantress could break the spell, but only at midnight.» What is the feminine word for enchanter? | Spellbinder | *Enchantress | Enchanted | Magician's hat
exercise: «Grandma is such an enchanter with her stories that we never want her to stop.» Does Grandma use real magic here? | Yes, she turns the room into a forest | *No, she charms and delights people with her stories | No, she is asleep | Yes, she is a wicked witch
test: «The knight rode through the forest to find the enchanter's tower.» Find and copy one word from the sentence that tells you the enchanter lives in a special place. | *tower | knight | rode | forest
test: «Her songs were so lovely that the whole crowd was enchanted.» Which word is closest in meaning to enchanter here, meaning someone who charms people? | Thief | *Charmer | Soldier | Cook
exam: Which sentence uses enchanter to mean someone who charms and delights people, not a magic person? | «The enchanter sealed the door with a spell.» | «Only the enchantress knew the secret word.» | *«Her smile was an enchanter, and everyone in the room felt happy.» | «The wicked enchanter turned the king to stone.»
